1
00:00:01,085 --> 00:00:05,340
Meet Bardic, the sound mixing table for game masters.

2
00:00:05,290 --> 00:00:10,547
Music, ambiences and sound effects to bring your tabletop RPG sessions to life.

3
00:00:10,497 --> 00:00:15,350
Each story is split into chapters, each with its own sounds.

4
00:00:17,128 --> 00:00:21,784
At the table, three zones: Music, Ambience and Events.

5
00:00:23,064 --> 00:00:27,919
Example: Underwater Adventure, chapter 1, “Chill on the beach”.

6
00:00:27,869 --> 00:00:33,925
Put your headphones on, close your eyes and let yourself drift away.

7
00:00:35,489 --> 00:00:46,539
First, the background music.

8
00:00:46,490 --> 00:00:56,541
Then the waves, brought in gently with the volume slider.

9
00:00:56,491 --> 00:01:07,041
A tropical day blends in.

10
00:01:08,993 --> 00:01:12,843
Finally, the events, right when the story calls for them.

11
00:01:12,793 --> 00:01:17,846
Footsteps in the sand

12
00:01:19,297 --> 00:01:23,347
A splash

13
00:01:26,298 --> 00:01:32,348
A ship's horn, far away

14
00:01:38,301 --> 00:01:42,852
You can open your eyes now.

15
00:01:47,974 --> 00:01:51,628
Creating your own story only takes a moment.

16
00:01:51,578 --> 00:02:00,629
Give it a name, then name your first chapter.

17
00:02:00,579 --> 00:02:17,911
Add sounds to each zone: from your files, or by reusing the ones already on your phone.

18
00:02:18,466 --> 00:02:23,519
To share it, tap Share: Bardic forges a .bardic file.

19
00:02:23,469 --> 00:02:28,520
Send it to another bard, who opens it with Import.

20
00:02:31,078 --> 00:02:37,129
The Compagnie des bardes is the Bardic community on the web.

21
00:02:38,937 --> 00:02:44,200
Its Story builder forges .bardic files from a computer.

22
00:02:45,972 --> 00:02:50,824
The Recueil gathers the stories shared by the bards.

23
00:02:50,774 --> 00:02:55,628
And you can lay your own tales in it too.

24
00:02:57,406 --> 00:03:02,962
Bardic is available on iPhone, on Android (beta) and on the web.

25
00:03:02,913 --> 00:03:08,466
Find it at arthurvangeersdaele.github.io/Bardic

